The message went through with a simple apology. Founder is right that the issue is the script formatting. Let me look at the script and figure out why `\n` appears as literal `\\n` in the output.

Looking at the script, the content field is constructed as:
```python
content = {
    "zh_cn": {
        "title": title,
        "content": [
            [
                {"tag": "at", "user_id": user_id},
                {"tag": "text", "text": f" {message}"}
            ]
        ]
    }
}
```

When the message has `\n` in it (as a literal string), the `f" {message}"` embeds it directly. 

The problem is that the post message format in Feishu expects actual newline characters within the text field, not escaped `\n` sequences. The f-string interpolation is just passing through the escape sequences as-is instead of interpreting them, so I need to either process the message with something like `textwrap.dedent` and `textwrap.fill`, or use a different approach to handle the actual line breaks before they get embedded in the JSON structure.

The cleanest solution would be to write a wrapper script that handles proper message formatting with real newlines and passes it to the Feishu API in a way that preserves the line breaks in the post content. I'll test sending a properly formatted multi-line message to see if the script can handle actual newlines instead of escape sequences.

